'.\" -*- nroff -*-
.TH KAFSDUMP 8 "2026-07-19" "kafs 0.4.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
kafsdump \- inspect offline KAFS image metadata without mutation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kafsdump
.RB [ --json ]
.I image
.br
.B kafsdump
.RB [ --json ]
.BI --recovery-log " log"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kafsdump
reads an offline KAFS image in read-only mode and prints a compact metadata summary.
The tool never writes image contents.
.PP
With
.BR --recovery-log ,
the input is a saved kafs-v7 mount log instead of an image.  The tool locates
and strictly validates the machine-readable controlled-admission recovery
record, then reports its resume stage and operation counters without modifying
the log.
.SH OUTPUT
The dump contains the following sections:
.TP
.B superblock
Magic/version, block geometry, free counters, and tail metadata region flags,
offset, and size.
.TP
.B tail_metadata
Tail metadata probe status and, when available, the region header summary
including container and slot counters. Empty format version 5 scaffold images
report this section as available with zero containers and zero live slots.
.TP
.B inode_summary
Inode totals, used/free counts, and number of in-use inodes with link count 0.
.TP
.B hrl_summary
HRL entry totals, live entry count, and refcount sum.
.TP
.B journal_header
In-image journal header fields and header CRC validation result.
.TP
.B metadata_regions
Offline metadata span summary used for SD-card wear diagnostics.
.TP
.B layout_descriptor
For accepted format version 7 images, selected version 2 K7LD generation and
geometry.  Version 1 pre-specification scaffolds fail the accepted-layout
boundary.
.TP
.B root_locators
Independent primary and tail K7SA status and locator selection.
.TP
.B descriptor_replicas
Per-copy role, offset, generation, CRC status, selection, and
valid/invalid/stale/divergent state.
.TP
.B checkpoints
Per-copy K7CP status and selected durable free-count baseline.
.TP
.B groups
Descriptor-owned metadata and logical/physical data spans.
.TP
.B shards
V7-owned type, storage class, logical coverage, and physical coverage records.
.TP
.B wear_distribution
Format v7 filesystem-level group placement policy, placement span/arena bytes,
and minimum/maximum group data-block counts.  This reports logical/physical
image address distribution; it does not infer flash translation layer or
physical erase-block wear.
.TP
.B journal_segments
Group-local rotating-header segment count, selected state, and checkpoint
sequence.
.PP
Format version 6 offline dumping has been retired.  Such images are rejected
with recreate-as-v7 guidance; no descriptor data or compatibility keys are
emitted.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --json
Emit machine-readable JSON instead of text output.  Accepted v7 output has the
stable top-level keys
.BR root_locators ,
.BR layout_descriptor ,
.BR descriptor_replicas ,
.BR checkpoints ,
.BR groups ,
.BR shards ,
.BR wear_distribution ,
and
.BR journal_segments .
.TP
.BI --recovery-log " log"
Inspect a saved kafs-v7 recovery log.  Missing, duplicate, unknown, malformed,
or out-of-range recovery fields cause validation failure.  In JSON mode the
validated record is emitted under the stable top-level
.B recovery
key.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Dump completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
I/O or format-boundary error.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kafs (1),
.BR kafsctl (1),
.BR mkfs.kafs (8),
.BR fsck.kafs (8),
.BR kafsimage (8),
.BR kafsresize (8),
.BR kafs-info (8)
.SH AUTHOR
kafs project.
